# pc-surf-key (BENCH-281): c is master, aa its A/A copy; kl plays the fitted surf keys (SKEY-2: nine key-weight multipliers
# and the kernel width) against the robots the fit shipped a key for, klbb the weights-only keys (width 1). bb only names
# the second build apart; it changes nothing.
c | hadur117.Hadur 3.25.1 | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.25.1.jar
aa | hadur117.Hadur 3.25.1aa | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.25.1aa.jar
kl | hadur117.Hadur 3.25.1kl | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.25.1kl.jar
klbb | hadur117.Hadur 3.25.1klbb | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.25.1klbb.jar
